claimed: chunk-size-representation — close the gap to ZIO on chunked merging. Ours gets SLOWER as the chunk grows (222/277/438us on 2x2000 at 16/256/1024) where ZIO's gets faster (127/75/75). Not stack depth (chunk-stack-safety's trampoline moved it not at all). Suspect the representation: Stage.chunked accumulates into a Vector and copies it into an ArraySeq per chunk, while this library already owns the right tool -- ChunkBuf, an opaque type over an existential array, measured 3-4x faster than ArrayBuffer/newBuilder paths, and documented for exactly the fill-across-pulls case. Watch for the replay hazard a mutable state introduces into a Free program.
